    "content": {
      "value": "Requirements extracted from Zimmermann Functional Requirements excel, downloaded July 3rd, 2026 after all requirements were confirmed. — source of truth. Req ID prefix: **HPC**.\n\n⚠️ **Rows with strikethrough are out of scope** — struck through in the Excel source file.\n\n|  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Req ID** | **Functional Area** | **Sub-Functional Area** | **Requirement** | **Status** | **Comments** | **User Stories** |\n| HPC-001 | Homepage & Content | Content Model & CMS Authoring | The system should serve all homepage content from Contentful as the sole CMS across all regional storefronts. | Confirmed | Open Discussion: Product Names/Prices - SFCC vs Contentful - Review with @Tim Lavelle  @Jasmijn Tsang | [https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=(text%20~%20%22HPC-001\\*%22%20or%20summary%20~%20%22HPC-001\\*%22%20or%20key%20%3D%20HPC-001)%20and%20project%20in%20(SFCC)%20ORDER%20BY%20created%20DESC](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=(text%20~%20%22HPC-001*%22%20or%20summary%20~%20%22HPC-001*%22%20or%20key%20%3D%20HPC-001)%20and%20project%20in%20(SFCC)%20ORDER%20BY%20created%20DESC) |\n| HPC-002 | Homepage & Content | Content Model & CMS Authoring | The system should provide a Contentful preview environment for authors to validate content before publishing to production. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-002> |\n| HPC-003 | Homepage & Content | Content Model & CMS Authoring | The system should manage all images and video assets through the CMS media library. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-003> |\n| HPC-004 | Homepage & Content | Content Model & CMS Authoring | The system should support videos referenced via embed URL within CMS content entries. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-004> |\n| HPC-005 | Homepage & Content | Content Model & CMS Authoring | The system should support locale-specific homepage content across all regional storefronts. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-005> |\n| HPC-006 | Homepage & Content | Content Model & CMS Authoring | The system should ingest translated content from Transperfect into the correct CMS locale fields upon delivery, triggered once content is marked as ready for translation. | Confirmed | EK - We need to discuss the translation strategy/ workflow.  Preference is for translation memory and workflow to live in the CMS, with an integration to Transperfect for human review. Review with @Tim Lavelle | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-006> |\n| HPC-007 | Homepage & Content | Content Model & CMS Authoring | The system should allow regional authors to publish locale-specific content without affecting other storefronts. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-007> |\n| /HPC-008 | Homepage & Content | Content Model & CMS Authoring | The system should support a full-width hero banner with CMS-managed imagery, copy and CTA links. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-008> |\n| HPC-009 | Homepage & Content | Content Model & CMS Authoring | The system should support editorial modules including campaign imagery, collection features and product spotlights. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-009> |\n| HPC-010 | Homepage & Content | Content Model & CMS Authoring | The system should support reusable page builder templates across page types. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-010> |\n| HPC-011 | Homepage & Content | Content Model & CMS Authoring | The system should support a global and local content model where some content is global (e.g. Sustainability, Fashion Show Hub pages) and some is localised (e.g. policy pages). | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-011> |\n| HPC-012 | Homepage & Content | Content Model & CMS Authoring | The system should support live stream embedding on editorial pages via a structured CMS solution, replacing the current approach of raw HTML code snippets. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-012> |\n| HPC-013 | Homepage & Content | Consent & Cookie Management | The system should grey out all site content and prevent interaction with all site elements when the Didomi consent notice is displayed. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-013> |\n| HPC-014 | Homepage & Content | Consent & Cookie Management | The system should remove the grey out effect and restore full site interactivity once the customer has completed the Didomi consent flow. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-014> |\n| HPC-015 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Header | The system should display a sticky global header visible at the top of the screen on all pages and devices. | Confirmed | Open Discussion: Header sticky / non-sticky - pending motion design as well @Jasmijn Tsang | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-015> |\n| HPC-016 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Header | The system should display the Zimmermann brand logo linking back to the homepage. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-016> |\n| HPC-017 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Header | The system should display a rotating promotional announcement banner above the header managed via the CMS. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-017> |\n| HPC-018 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Header | The system should display the following clickable icons in the header: Locate Boutique, Contact Us, Newsletter, Search, Account and Bag. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-017> |\n| HPC-019 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Header | The system should display a Wishlist icon that navigates anonymous customers to the login page. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-019> |\n| HPC-020 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Header | The system should display a Wishlist icon that navigates logged in customers to the wishlist page. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-020> |\n| HPC-021 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Header | The system should display a Bag icon with a running count of items in the customer's bag. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-021> |\n| HPC-022 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Header | The system should display top-level navigation categories linking to the relevant product listing pages. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-022> |\n| HPC-023 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Header | The systems should display a 'Back in Boutique' navigation category to show customer items that will be in the boutique | Confirmed | Additional Notes: this is a manually created category by content team  @Jasmijn Tsang | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-023> |\n| HPC-024 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Header | The system will display a mega menu on desktop when a customer hovers over a navigation category, with the exception of Z.Immerse which will function as a direct link to a page | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-024> |\n| HPC-025 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Header | The system should display a hamburger menu on mobile to access navigation categories. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-025> |\n| HPC-026 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Header | The system should display a country/region selector in the header to allow customers to switch locale and country excluding the AU store. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-026> |\n| HPC-027 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Header | The system should persist the customer's selected region across sessions. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-027> |\n| HPC-028 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Header | The system should allow the business user to add and remove navigation items without requiring a code change. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-028> |\n| HPC-029 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Header | The system should support cloning of the global navigation structure across markets. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-029> |\n| HPC-030 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Footer | The system should display a global footer with content managed via the CMS. | Confirmed | Footer edibility per storefront | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-030> |\n| HPC-031 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Footer | The system should display footer navigation links. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-031> |\n| HPC-032 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Footer | The system should navigate the customer to the relevant page or destination when a footer link is clicked. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-032> |\n| HPC-033 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Footer | The system should display copyright and legal text in the footer. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-033> |\n| HPC-034 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Footer | The system should display a \"Join Us\" email capture field in the footer. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-034> |\n| HPC-035 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Footer | The system should display a modal on clicking the Continue CTA to collect the customer's first name and last name. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-035> |\n| HPC-036 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Footer | The system should pass email sign-up data to Omneo (who will then pass to Emarsys) | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-036> |\n| HPC-037 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Footer | The system should display appropriate privacy consent copy and a link to the local Privacy Policy on the sign-up modal. | Confirmed | Additional Note: Should display Accessibility  @Jasmijn Tsang | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-037> |\n| HPC-038 | Homepage & Content | Navigation — Footer | The system should allow business users to add region specific footer links (e.g Acknowledgement of Country for AU storefront). | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-038> |\n|  | Homepage & Content | Chat Integration | The system should display the chat widget as a pop-up overlay on the relevant pages. Page visibility rules are determined by Inside Chat. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-039> |\n| HPC-040 | Homepage & Content | Chat Integration | The system should only initialise the chat widget after the customer has consented to the relevant cookie category via Didomi. | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPRD-040> |",
